  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study visit urban water management (Part II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This incoming study visit of 10-12 municipal officers and stakeholders of education institutes from South African (SA) cities Durban, Cape Town and Johannesburg will introduce these officials to the Dutch triple helix cooperation in the water sector. The selected officials are related to the Orange Knowledge Programme (OKP) proposal on urban water technology under development by SA officials with Dutch education institutes. This study visit will also enhance the connections of these officials with Dutch educational and knowledge institutions and business partners within the Dutch Triple Helix. This visit will also aid in developing the eventual OKP proposal, which will be formulated concurrently. Additionally, it will allow them to engage with Dutch water technology experts identified in the technology needs assessment of PSD Apps, establish new collaborations, and initiate potential pilot projects in SA.</narrative>
  </description>
